WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.327
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.627 --> 00:00:09.013
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.313 --> 00:00:16.041
Unit eleven: Strategic Planning. Today you will articulate plans and intentions with future forms (will / going to).

4
00:00:16.341 --> 00:00:19.202
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:23.434
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.283 --> 00:00:25.644
Strategic planning.

7
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:31.517
Strategic planning means defining long-term direction and how resources will achieve it.

8
00:00:32.117 --> 00:00:35.486
Strategic planning aligned the ministry's budget with its goals.

9
00:00:36.083 --> 00:00:38.968
Your turn. Say: Strategic planning.

10
00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:43.206
Strategic planning.

11
00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:44.754
Vision.

12
00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:49.154
Vision means an inspiring statement of a desired future.

13
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:53.212
The university's vision is to become a regional research leader.

14
00:00:53.817 --> 00:00:56.515
Your turn. Say: Vision.

15
00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:00.147
Vision.

16
00:01:00.883 --> 00:01:01.954
Objective.

17
00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:05.611
Objective means a specific, measurable aim.

18
00:01:06.217 --> 00:01:11.084
Our first objective is to train 500 teachers by 2028.

19
00:01:11.683 --> 00:01:14.626
Your turn. Say: Objective.

20
00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:18.445
Objective.

21
00:01:19.183 --> 00:01:20.660
SWOT analysis.

22
00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:26.691
SWOT analysis means an assessment of strengths, weaknesses, opportunities and threats.

23
00:01:27.283 --> 00:01:31.024
The SWOT analysis revealed an overlooked opportunity in tourism.

24
00:01:31.617 --> 00:01:34.780
Your turn. Say: SWOT analysis.

25
00:01:37.633 --> 00:01:39.157
SWOT analysis.

26
00:01:39.917 --> 00:01:40.941
Milestone.

27
00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:45.772
Milestone means a significant checkpoint in progress toward a goal.

28
00:01:46.383 --> 00:01:49.660
Opening the first clinic was the project's key milestone.

29
00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:52.519
Your turn. Say: Milestone.

30
00:01:55.367 --> 00:01:56.345
Milestone.

31
00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.537
Resource allocation.

32
00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:04.290
Resource allocation means deciding how money, people and time are distributed.

33
00:02:04.883 --> 00:02:07.986
Resource allocation favoured rural schools this year.

34
00:02:08.583 --> 00:02:11.932
Your turn. Say: Resource allocation.

35
00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.360
Resource allocation.

36
00:02:17.117 --> 00:02:18.512
Long-term goal.

37
00:02:19.517 --> 00:02:23.304
Long-term goal means an aim to be achieved over several years.

38
00:02:23.917 --> 00:02:27.193
Our long-term goal is universal access to clean water.

39
00:02:27.783 --> 00:02:30.656
Your turn. Say: Long-term goal.

40
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.405
Long-term goal.

41
00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:38.314
Execution.

42
00:02:39.317 --> 00:02:42.013
Execution means the carrying out of a plan.

43
00:02:42.617 --> 00:02:45.382
A plan without execution is merely a wish.

44
00:02:45.983 --> 00:02:48.729
Your turn. Say: Execution.

45
00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:52.591
Execution.

46
00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:57.329
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:58.183 --> 00:03:04.365
Visal, the provincial hospital has a beautiful five-year plan, but nothing seems to change. Why?

48
00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:15.695
Because the plan states hopes rather than commitments. 'We hope to improve care' is vague; 'We will open two new wards by 2027' is accountable.

49
00:03:16.783 --> 00:03:18.678
So the language itself matters?

50
00:03:19.783 --> 00:03:30.797
Very much. 'Will' signals decisions and promises, while 'going to' signals plans already in motion: 'We're going to recruit ten nurses next quarter.'

51
00:03:31.883 --> 00:03:33.662
And how do they keep on track?

52
00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:44.217
With milestones. Each quarter, they'll measure progress, and if they're behind, they will reallocate resources toward the weakest areas.

53
00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:46.809
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:51.600
Grammar focus: Future planning language (will, going to).

55
00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:53.133
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:53.817 --> 00:03:56.548
We will allocate resources toward this milestone.

57
00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.506
The hospital is going to recruit ten nurses next quarter.

58
00:04:01.417 --> 00:04:04.879
Each quarter, we will measure progress against our objectives.

59
00:04:05.833 --> 00:04:17.878
In strategic documents, 'will' expresses firm commitments and predictions; 'be going to' presents plans already decided or evidence-based predictions. Avoid vague verbs like 'hope to' or 'try to' when you mean a commitment.

60
00:04:18.617 --> 00:04:22.604
Be careful! Don't say: We going to allocate more funds.

61
00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:27.332
Say: We are going to allocate more funds.

62
00:04:27.632 --> 00:04:28.982
Be + going to.

63
00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:32.349
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:34.808
From Vision to Execution.

65
00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:41.473
Strategic planning translates an organisation's vision into concrete objectives, priorities and timelines.

66
00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:50.817
A typical process begins with a SWOT analysis, which clarifies internal strengths and weaknesses as well as external opportunities and threats.

67
00:04:51.833 --> 00:04:59.406
Effective plans then specify who will do what, by when, and with which resources, rather than relying on general aspirations.

68
00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:07.067
Milestones allow leaders to monitor progress and adjust resource allocation before small delays become major failures.

69
00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:16.591
Studies repeatedly show, however, that most strategies fail in execution rather than in design, so communication and accountability are critical.

70
00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:22.073
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:22.917 --> 00:05:25.732
Look at those clouds! It blank rain.

72
00:05:26.032 --> 00:05:29.824
A, will. B, is going to. C, going to.

73
00:05:33.367 --> 00:05:35.506
The answer is B: is going to.

74
00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:41.146
An assessment of strengths, weaknesses, opportunities and threats is a blank.

75
00:05:41.446 --> 00:05:45.447
A, SWOT analysis. B, milestone. C, vision.

76
00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.615
The answer is A: SWOT analysis.

77
00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:56.154
Deciding how money, people and time are distributed is blank.

78
00:05:56.454 --> 00:06:01.095
A, execution. B, objective. C, resource allocation.

79
00:06:04.633 --> 00:06:07.538
The answer is C: resource allocation.

80
00:06:08.683 --> 00:06:10.787
Choose the most accountable sentence.

81
00:06:11.087 --> 00:06:20.348
A, We hope to maybe improve results.. B, We will raise pass rates by 10% by 2027.. C, We try improving results sometime..

82
00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:29.429
The answer is B: We will raise pass rates by 10% by 2027..

83
00:06:30.583 --> 00:06:33.442
According to the reading, most strategies fail in…

84
00:06:33.742 --> 00:06:38.104
A, design. B, execution. C, SWOT analysis.

85
00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:44.049
The answer is B: execution.

86
00:06:45.233 --> 00:06:48.640
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:49.483 --> 00:06:53.898
What is one long-term goal you have, and what milestone would show progress?

88
00:07:10.683 --> 00:07:12.149
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:07:12.449 --> 00:07:47.512
One of my long-term goals is to become a qualified translator between Khmer and English, specialising in legal documents. I am going to begin by completing an advanced certificate next year, which will be my first milestone. After that, I will gain practical experience by volunteering for an NGO that needs translations. A second milestone would be passing a professional accreditation exam within three years. Measuring progress this way will keep me accountable and motivated.

90
00:07:47.812 --> 00:07:49.673
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:50.583 --> 00:07:55.848
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and future planning language (will, going to).

92
00:07:56.148 --> 00:08:01.169
Today's value is strategic thinking. Think ahead, and choose your path with purpose.

93
00:08:01.469 --> 00:08:04.167
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

94
00:08:04.467 --> 00:08:07.932
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

